1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,440
It'd been rained on for weeks and chewed up by coyotes.

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:05,790
The only other DNA other than the vic's was some bear semen found in the hair.

3
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:06,130
Right.

4
00:00:06,270 --> 00:00:06,710
Who found the body?

5
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:08,000
Hikers.

6
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:09,450
You're really going to just blow past the bear semen detail?

7
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:12,690
I imagine a bear mistook the rotting corpse for a female of its species

8
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:14,140
and had intercourse with it.

9
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:14,970
Nothing I haven't seen before.

10
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:15,630
It isn't?

11
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:16,210
Let's get in here.

12
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:17,310
Start working this guy.

13
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:17,830
Oh.

14
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:19,830
You're gonna come in with me.

15
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:22,350
I just thought maybe you'd watch from out here,

16
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,290
you know, pull me out when I'm getting too hot.

17
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:25,230
Call me a loose cannon.

18
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:26,630
You know, classic Captain stuff.

19
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:30,010
Peralta, do you know what I miss most about being a detective?

20
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:32,000
A good interrogation.

21
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,450
Breaking suspects down.

22
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:36,070
Talking quietly and then talking real loud.

23
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,850
Looking away and then looking right in their eyes.

24
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:45,000
Leaning.

25
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:44,750
That was amazing.

26
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:46,070
So, can I join you?

27
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:49,690
Well, a lot of these techniques do work better with two people:

28
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:50,810
you know, good cop bad cop,

29
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:55,670
crazy cop sane cop, fast talking streetwise cop and Hong Kong cop, AKA the Rush Hour.

30
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:56,110
You know what?

31
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:56,550
Let's do this.

32
00:00:56,650 --> 00:00:57,750
Let's break this son of a bitch!

33
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,010
Hello, Philip.

34
00:01:02,330 --> 00:01:02,410
Detective.

35
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:04,230
This is Captain Raymond Holt.

36
00:01:04,490 --> 00:01:06,890
a bit of a legend in interrogation Hey, Cap,

37
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:09,130
who's the scariest person you've ever gotten a confession out of?

38
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:09,950
Connie Buttons.

39
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:12,890
Okay, thought it was gonna sound a little cooler, but no matter.

40
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:16,930
So, shall we recap the night that Robert Tupper was murdered Friday the 22nd?

41
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:19,130
I believe you were the last person to see him alive, correct?

42
00:01:19,290 --> 00:01:19,610
No.

43
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,150
I'd imagine whoever killed him so I'm not that...

44
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:23,030
Ooh, nice dodge.

45
00:01:23,550 --> 00:01:24,730
You're quick, like a cat.

46
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:25,770
Like a dancer.

47
00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:26,850
Like Great Tiger.

48
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:29,490
From Mike Tyson's Punch Out.

49
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:30,730
He could teleport around the ring.
